        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed the issue in `top-picks.tsx`, but I couldn't confirm it with the linter: running oxlint needed approval, which isn't available in this run.\n\n**The fix:** at `top-picks.tsx:327`, each color swatch `<button>` contained only an empty decorative `<div>`, so it had no text label. I added `aria-label={color}` to the button. This is what the rule's help text asks for, so I expect the diagnostic to clear. It matches the existing `title={color}`, so screen readers now announce the swatch by its color value (for example `#1e1e1e` or `transparent`). Nothing else changed, and the button behaves the same at runtime.\n\nIf you'd rather have a friendlier spoken label than the raw color value, you could use a translation through the `t()` helper the file already uses. I didn't add one because I couldn't check which translation keys exist without looking at other files.",
